-connections were logged out mid-checkout and lost their pantry orders.
+For whoever changes login or the session expiry, revokes a stolen phone's access, or answers a member who was logged
+out. A session keeps a member logged in until logout or 30 minutes pass without a request. The limit was 10 minutes
+until 2024, when members on slow mobile connections were logged out mid-checkout and lost their pantry orders.
 
 ## Lifetime
 
@@ -14,6 +14,23 @@ minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 ## Storage
 
 Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The schema is [sessions.sql](../../larder/sessions.sql). Install `requirements.txt`, set `DATABASE_URL` to the shared
+Postgres database, and apply that schema before starting the web servers. Every server must use the same
+`LARDER_SESSION_KEY`.
+
+## Logout
+
+A member's phone was stolen while they were logged in. Volunteers can call `logout(member_id)` in
+[sessions.py](../../larder/sessions.py) to revoke all that member's sessions immediately. Once the call returns,
+subsequent verification rejects their existing cookies on every server. Other members stay logged in, and the
+affected member can log in again to create a new session. Repeating logout is safe, including for an unknown member.
+Already authorized requests are not cancelled.
+
+## Known limits
+
+Cookies issued before database session records were introduced are rejected; those members must log in again.
+Database failures propagate to the caller: a volunteer must retry a failed logout, and requests must not treat a
+verification error as authenticated access.
 
